  "problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$",
  "worked_solution": "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0=4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first equation is a false statement. Hence,the system has no solution.",
